   Presumably you're trying to take a *matrix* square root (i.e. find a
matrix C = B^(-1/2)  such that C C^T = B^(-1), or C C^T B = identity matrix?

   There are many matrix square roots (it's not a uniquely defined
operation), although the most widely used options (e.g. Cholesky
decomposition) don't work (IIRC) for non-square matrices.

   If you're trying to take *elementwise* square roots then you can loop
over the elements and take the square root of each one ...

   Can you say a little bit more about the context in which this formula
occurs?

