Dear Ben

Thanks for your answer!
Of course, here an image about the main idea to develop:

If you see, the expression for L is in function of sigma2(hat), lambda (hat), B and K. The authors don't mention what type of matrix is (square roots or another) but as you say, use the Cholesky decomposition doesn't work here.
I followed this example in R (http://menugget.blogspot.com/2012/03/exponentiation-of-matrix-including.html) and it works. However, I would like to create that same matrix B^-1/2 in TMB to get my sparse matrix L.

Best wishes

